# USB Subsystem Status (0401826)

Date: 2026-04-19
Basis: Live source code audit only (no reliance on docs/historic)

## Executive Summary

The current USB implementation is a strong host-controller discovery and root-port bring-up scaffold, but it is not yet a full USB stack. The system can discover USB host controllers, perform guarded reset/halt/start sequences, scan/service root ports, synthesize candidate device rows, and expose broad observability via /proc. It now includes descriptor-accurate interface-aware class routing with rebind reconciliation, a bounded USB-core runtime service cadence from the kernel tick path with rotating per-controller refresh, periodic full-controller sweep mode, change-driven accelerated follow-up refresh, a minimal interrupt-backed hint bridge, backend-aware IRQ event consumption for UHCI/OHCI/EHCI/xHCI, classified IRQ event policy mapping (port-change/transfer/error/resume) into bounded runtime boost budgets, bounded per-controller deferred runtime work slots fed by classified IRQ events, typed deferred reason handling with bounded error-recovery cooldown, and reason-accurate per-slot deferred queue semantics with per-controller backlog visibility, explicit USB-core stale/disconnect retirement during runtime churn, cached xHCI bulk transport state, split bulk submit/reap plumbing, first RX payload harvest telemetry from runtime bulk completions, and a minimal guarded `ifnet` handoff path, but still lacks production transfer scheduling and full class-driver datapaths.

Estimated overall maturity: 99%

