## Practical Next Step

Immediate best next implementation target is reason-specific execution behavior:
- Route typed deferred reasons into differentiated refresh actions (for example, selective re-enumeration paths vs lightweight rescan paths) instead of one generic refresh call.
- Use the new per-controller deferred backlog tuple to tune reason-specific queue caps and cooldown policy by controller kind.
- Follow with device-specific control/register access needed to get beyond descriptor-only identification.

Follow-up target after that:
- Expand composite-device and altsetting-aware policy so class routing remains correct once more USB families are exercised.

That sequence is the shortest path from cached/polled transport pulses to a real running USB network datapath.
